[node name="MapBase" parent="." instance=ExtResource("10_map_model")]
editor_description = "maps/marble/models/marble.glb: the whole rotunda, one contiguous mesh -- the spiked ground floor at y -1.0, the gallery walkway r 46.7..59.55 at y 23.0 with its open inner lip, the seven tiers of barred cells (bases -1/7/15/23/31/39/47), the wall top at 55, the dome from 57.8 to the apex at 84.8. Ships its own collision (MarbleCollision-colonly); the spikes are not in it, the volumes kill first."

[node name="KillBox" type="Area3D" parent="."]
editor_description = "The catch-all under the whole map, roof at y -3.0 and 30 m deep (to y -33.0): nothing should ever reach it (the lowest floor is the spiked ground floor at y -1.0, and SpikeFloor already covers everything down to -3.0), so a body here fell through the world. Trigger only, mask 1048577 (living bodies and ghosts); scripts/match/kill_volume.gd hands whatever entered to MatchController.handle_fall()."
transform = Transform3D(1, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 5, 0)
collision_layer = 0
collision_mask = 1048577
monitorable = false
script = ExtResource("1_kill_volume")
radius_metres = 64.0
roof_depth_metres = 8.0
depth_metres = 30.0

[node name="Shape" type="CollisionShape3D" parent="KillBox"]
editor_description = "Deliberately empty. KillVolume._build_shape writes a CylinderShape3D over it on ready."

[node name="SpikeFloor" type="Area3D" parent="."]
editor_description = "THE SPIKED GROUND FLOOR: a thin slab at the pit floor, r 47.0 (the inner tiers' wall face is 47.15), y -1.0 up to 2.0 -- just over the spike tips (tallest 2.2 m cone on a 0.12 plinth, tips within y 2.42 of the floor's -1.0 reference, the slab's roof catches the body's feet well before its hips). A body leaves the walkway lip, falls the full 24 m and dies on the spikes; nothing above y 2.0 kills. The tower's shaft is inside the disc but no body is. The spikes themselves are not colliders."
transform = Transform3D(1, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 10, 0)
collision_layer = 0
collision_mask = 1048577
monitorable = false
script = ExtResource("1_kill_volume")
radius_metres = 47.0
roof_depth_metres = 8.0
depth_metres = 3.0

[node name="Shape" type="CollisionShape3D" parent="SpikeFloor"]

[node name="StartEnd" type="Node3D" parent="."]
editor_description = "One level, one lap: start at 5 deg and finish at 345 deg on the lane at y 23.0, the bars at 353 deg between them. Nothing else stands on the run: with the course gone it is 340 deg of clear gallery from the start to the gate."

[node name="PrisonerStart" type="Marker3D" parent="StartEnd"]
editor_description = "5.0 deg on the lane, y 23.0: the model's lane surface exactly. Its ANGLE places the field -- MatchController deals bodies radially across the lane from here at start_line_spacing_metres -- and its height is load-bearing."
transform = Transform3D(-0.996195, 0, 0.0871557, 0, 1, 0, -0.0871557, 0, -0.996195, 51.8021, 23, 4.5321)

[node name="PrisonerEnd" type="Marker3D" parent="StartEnd"]
editor_description = "345.0 deg on the lane, matching the portal's own transform. The end of the whole route: reaching it takes the tower."
transform = Transform3D(0.965926, 0, 0.258819, 0, 1, 0, -0.258819, 0, 0.965926, 50.2281, 23, -13.4586)

[node name="Portal" parent="StartEnd" instance=ExtResource("19_portal")]
editor_description = "The finish at 345 deg. maps/marble/props/marble_portal.tscn -- portal.tscn node for node, the same Glow and the same Gate in the finish_gate group, with the marble surround in place of the hell-rock arch and the portal's own effect surface unchanged inside it. Local Z is the pass-through axis along the run, local X the span across the lane."
transform = Transform3D(0.965926, 0, 0.258819, 0, 1, 0, -0.258819, 0, 0.965926, 50.2281, 23, -13.4586)


[node name="Bars" parent="." instance=ExtResource("20_marble_bars")]
editor_description = "Bars across the walkway at 353 deg, in the gap between finish (345) and start (5), and the ONE fixture that survived the clearing of the lane (Ryan, 2026-09-22: \"get rid of all the elements on the ring\") -- because the bake and the harness say it is not decoration. With a finish gate in the scene, standing in it is the win (MatchLapTracker: no checkpoints), so without these bars RingBake links PrisonerStart to PrisonerEnd the SHORT way round, 18.06 m backwards through this gap instead of 288.15 m forwards, and a bot runner walks straight to the portal: 7 of 10 harness matches went unresolved at 101-129 one-shot rounds. With them, 10 of 10 resolve. They stand outside the 340 deg run, behind the finish, so they are in no shot of the lane. maps/marble/models/marble_bars.glb: an iron portcullis in a marble frame in the rotunda's own architecture -- ashlar plinth, fluted pilaster jambs, a 6.00 x 6.20 m mouth under a semicircular head, a cornice moulding -- the iron the same near-black as the cell bars. IT SPANS THE WALKWAY WALL TO LIP (Ryan, 2026-09-23: \"the gate doesnt block anyone from going past it to the portal\"). It did not: on rock_bars' inherited 10.6 m centred on the lane at r 52.0 the collider reached r 46.7007..57.3005, and the walkway runs r 46.7..59.55 -- 2.2495 m of open floor outboard of the gate, measured headless off this scene, and a body walked ROUND it to the portal rather than through it. The gate is now 12.85 m wide and its centre stands at r 53.125, so the collider reaches the inner lip and the cell wall and there is no floor left to walk round; the extra 2.25 m went into the flanking ashlar field, mouth, jambs and bars all unchanged. Everything else is still rock_bars': 8.5 m tall, origin the base centre, and no gap anywhere wider than 0.38 m. Local X (12.85 m) runs radially across the lane, local Z along it. tests/test_marble_gate.gd drives a capsule at it from across the whole walkway and is what says it holds."
transform = Transform3D(0.992546, 0, 0.121869, 0, 1, 0, -0.121869, 0, 0.992546, 52.729014, 23, -6.474309)

[node name="Watch" type="Node3D" parent="."]
editor_description = "Where the AI guard's scan rests when it has nothing remembered: five points spread round the lap, so the crosshair sweeps the lane instead of staring at one bearing. Markers only -- nothing is drawn and nothing collides. They are all the Sections node left behind when the course came off the lane (Ryan, 2026-09-22: \"for the marble level, can you just get rid of all the elements on the ring?\"), kept because they are not an element ON the ring: deleting them would change how the guard plays, which is not what was asked. Named by bearing now that there are no stretches to name them after."

